If a patient has a renal-insufficiency then every clinician should heed an additional-opioid-caution for the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
If a patient has a hepatic-insufficiency then every clinician should heed an additional-opioid-caution for the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
If a patient is an older-adult then every clinician should heed an additional-opioid-caution for the patient and should increase a patient-monitoring for the patient and should minimize an opioid-risk for the patient.
